# The class side's own conformance (#733, PR 1; generated): target x the
# path of what implements the requirement x module arguments, each cell
# printing what runs for the abstract class method `R.label` through
# `Type[R]`, through `T <: R` and by a direct call. The class includes `O`
# (which includes `R`) itself; what implements `R.label` is, by the rule
# (`World::class_method_target`, the instance side's witness over the
# class object's dispatch order): the first class method of the
# signature in that order, its own class methods, its own includes (the
# last first), the modules of its top-level unconditional extensions, then
# its superclass's in the same way; a subclass inherits it. Expected
# output computed from that rule, not from a run: `own` prints the class's
# own, `B` the superclass's, `E` the module that gives it.
# Skipped as identical by the rules or not expressible:
# - scoped or conditional extension paths: their modules are no
#   implementation of the class's own side (rule A), refused
#   (diagnostics.rs, a_class_method_of_another_parameter_type_is_no_implementation)
# - another cog's extension: a library never adds to a class from outside
#   it (10-cogs.md), so its modules are not on the class's dispatch
# - an extension of the included module `O`: an extension of a module
#   includes nothing (#609)
# - module target: a module has no class object to call
# - abstract target x sub paths: the abstract target's cells already run
#   on its concrete subclass
# - args param x non-generic targets: no class parameter to pass
# - generic target x args none/concrete: the class parameter goes unused,
#   as the class cells
module R1
  abstract def self.label -> String
end
module O1
  include R1
end
module E1
  def self.label -> String = "E"
end
class B1
  def initialize; end
end
class X1 < B1
  include O1
  def initialize; end
  def self.label -> String = "own"
end
def f1(t: Type[R1]) -> String = t.label
def g1[T <: R1](t: Type[T]) -> String = t.label
puts "class/own/none: #{f1(X1)} #{g1(X1)} #{X1.label}"
